// =============================================================================
//  probe_session.hml — AN HOUR, MEASURED, AND THE HOUR IT REPLACES
// =============================================================================
//
//      hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_session.hml -o /tmp/probe_session
//      /tmp/probe_session                         # COMPILED — the shipping path
//      /tmp/probe_session --seeds 3 --sweep 20    # a shorter seed sweep
//      nm /tmp/probe_session | grep -c SDL_       # MUST be 0
//
//  Exits 1 on any failed assertion and asserts its own assertion COUNT, so a
//  section that silently stops running is a FAILURE rather than a green run.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  It runs ONE FULL HOUR of game time — 3600 s, 216 000 ticks, 3.75 of the
//  16-minute day — through the REAL server and the REAL client, and samples
//  thirty-two numbers once per game minute.  The output is a minute-by-minute
//  account of what the player has, and the whole point of it is that the
//  columns STOP MOVING somewhere, and this file says where.
//
//  THE_HOUR.md and THE_HOUR_2.md are the two hours it has measured so far.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  THE TWO ARMS, AND WHY THEY ARE NOW THE SAME FILE WITH ONE SWITCH
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Both arms are `src/game/demobot.hml`, THE SHIPPING DRIVER, imported and not
//  ported.  The lesson of `probe_firstminute` is that a port is how "10 of 12"
//  and "0 of 8" became two truths about one game, and the previous version of
//  this file re-learned it the hard way: its ARM WALK was a SECOND town driver
//  living in a probe, it broke at 26:00, and THE_HOUR_2 §4.3 had to write
//  "any future use of ARM WALK should be treated as unmeasured after minute 26".
//
//  So there is one driver now and the arms are a boolean on it:
//
//  ARM LAMP — `demobot_set_errand(b, 1)`, the DEFAULT, i.e. exactly what
//      `main.hml --demo 3600` does on a display.  It holds the post through the
//      night, walks home at dawn, plants its lantern kits inside the ring the
//      HUD draws, talks to every named villager who is home, presses every row
//      of their shop, and walks back out.  This is the hour the game is.
//
//  ARM HOLD — `demobot_set_errand(b, 0)`.  The errand layer stops running and
//      what is left is the driver that SHIPPED BEFORE THIS WAVE, byte for byte,
//      because the combat pass in `demobot.hml` was not touched.  It leashes to
//      the first lantern post at 16 m and never leaves.  This is the CONTROL,
//      and it is what makes every LAMP number above a difference rather than a
//      claim.
//
//  THE ORACLE, DECLARED, AND IT IS SMALLER THAN IT WAS.  The old ARM WALK read
//  villager positions from `npc_x`/`npc_z` AND the settlement centre from
//  `settle_cx`.  The driver now navigates on `client_settle_x`/`client_settle_z`
//  (the compass diamond) and decides where a post counts from
//  `client_settle_inside` (the ring the teach-the-verb work draws on the ground
//  when you are carrying a wick) — both are on the wire and both are on the
//  screen.  The ONE remaining server read is villager position, because
//  `client.hml` publishes none; `demobot.hml`'s header declares it and names
//  `main.hml:1240`, which reads the same two functions to DRAW them.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  WHAT THIS FILE STOPPED MEASURING, AND WHY THAT IS NOT A WEAKENING
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  THE SHADOW SETTLEMENT IS RETIRED.  It ran a private copy of `settle.hml` fed
//  from `w.anim` instead of `w.model` to measure what the one-word fix in
//  `sv_lan_gather` would buy.  That fix landed in `b996b41`; THE_HOUR_2 §6
//  recorded the counterfactual and the ship agreeing at 7 rows each.  A
//  counterfactual whose fact has landed is not a measurement, it is a copy of
//  `settle.hml` that has to be kept in sync with `settle.hml` forever.  The six
//  assertions it carried are replaced by twelve that measure the loop the fix
//  made possible — including the first unfixtured talk and the first unfixtured
//  trade this repository has ever recorded.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  IMPORTS — this is a tool, so the wall (CLAUDE.md §3) permits src/game/**.
//  It links NO SDL and NO wobbleweed, and `nm | grep -c SDL_` must print 0.
// =============================================================================

